## 6. Current subsystem boundaries

### `DiskManager`

Owns process-local file descriptors and positional page I/O.

Does not understand persisted object/page formats.

### `PageFile`

Owns page-file lifecycle, superblock identity validation, and append-first physical page allocation.

Does not own buffer frames or normal buffered page lifetime.

### `Page`

Owns exactly one in-memory 8192-byte page buffer plus `PageId`.

Does not contain BufferPool metadata.

### `HeapPage`

Non-owning page-local controller.

Owns physical heap-page validation and mutations only.

Treats tuple payload as opaque bytes.

Does not decide SQL/MVCC visibility or global reclamation eligibility.

### `TuplePhysicalLayout` / `TupleCodec`

Own schema-directed physical tuple layout and serialization.

Do not perform storage I/O and do not depend on BufferPool/HeapFile.

### `FsmPage`

Non-owning controller for one persisted `FSM_DATA` page.

Performs no file/page I/O itself.

### `FsmCandidateIndex`

Rebuildable runtime advisory candidate index.

Performs no storage I/O and does not inspect live heap pages.

### Future `HeapFile`

Not implemented.

Must coordinate relation-wide page access through BufferPool rather than bypassing it with direct `DiskManager` access.

