## 8. Open architecture follow-up

### RID reserved bytes, persisted bytes 14..15

Current implementation:

```text
EncodeRid:
    writes bytes 14..15 as zero

DecodeRid:
    currently ignores bytes 14..15
```

The Phase 1 audit identified this as the only unresolved architecture question.

Proposed future synchronization:

```text
RID v1 reserved bytes:
    encoder MUST write zero
    decoder MUST reject nonzero
```

This is **not yet treated as newly locked by this state file**.

Until `ARCHITECTURE.md` is explicitly updated, do not silently change the decoder solely because this proposal appears here.

Compatibility note:

Database-produced encoded RIDs already contain zero reserved bytes. Tightening decoding would only reject previously tolerated/external 16-byte inputs containing nonzero reserved bytes.

